strong words from the governor and the  department of education  calling ccsd superintendent dr jesus  jarrah quote dishonest  this all has to do with the issue of  school funding oracle mana has more on  what's causing the controversy and how  ccsd is responding governor steve  sisolak and superintendent of public  instruction  joan ebert are not mincing words this  all revolves around statements made by  ccsd superintendent  dr jesus dara about assembly bill 2. the  bill would have let the school district  take leftover money from schools and  give it to the district  to help with the budget crisis right now  the nevada legislature is in a special  session  figuring out ways to deal with the  state's 1.2 billion dollar budget hole  dr jarrah had said the agenda item came  from a request  from the state department of education  but state leaders say jarrah is  misleading the public  the governor said in part quote being  superintendent of one of the largest  school districts in the nation requires  leadership  and leadership requires honesty  unfortunately that is not what we get  from superintendent jarrah  clark county students staff and family  members deserve better  superintendent ebert also said in part  quote it is incredibly concerning that  superintendent jarrah is again blaming  the state  for his actions instead of taking  responsibility for ccsd's request to  sweep funds  from individual schools to cover the  district's funding deficit  now this is what dr jarrett said at a  virtual town hall yesterday when asked  about assembly bill 2.  let me just clarify because there was  never support as i stated  in the state assembly in the senate and  the assembly  i was very clear that i was going to  work collaboratively with the building  principals to  to balance the budget it was not the  recommendation and it was not ccsd  bill the bill was not ccsd's bill  ab2 assembly bill 2 was presented to  lawmakers over the weekend it's unclear  if it'll move forward we just got this  statement from ccsd on behalf of dr  jarrah he says in part quote i want to  work hand in hand with our state leaders  to find the right solutions  for maintaining fiscal responsibility  while at the same time giving our  children  and their families what they need to be  successful  it is in all of our best interests to  work together and that is my goal but we  have to get to a place  of true collaboration to read the full  statements from dr  jarrah governor sisilak and  superintendent ebert go to 8newsnow.com  in the newsroom orca mana 8 news now
 

